{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 4e8cf844: confirmed. R3a covers the four signer-key structures only. The admitted, kept and retained maps each hold at most 4,096 admitted keys, beside the 4,096-entry FIFO of revoked keys that were never admitted, with generation invalidation of outstanding signer standings. Do not edit the Further.read reusable map (authority.ts:145) in R3a. The docs say \"signer-key memory\", not all observation memory.\n\nOne addition to R3a's implementation note: state which inputs choose the subject names that Further.read stores. If an act's content can name an arbitrary subject, a caller can grow that map without limit, the same class of defect as the signer-key bound. In that case, add one sentence to the threat-model residual paragraph naming that map as unbounded, and I file a separate request for it. If only definitions name those subjects, a definition bounds the map, and the note says so.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}